{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/106079-kept-stigmatics","id":106079,"title":"Kept Stigmatics?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-04-04T23:54:15-07:00","id":106079,"title":"Kept Stigmatics?","content":"Any awesome opinions regarding what happens when one of the Gentry steal a stigmatic away?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thread Reaper <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Roboto\">\uff1c(\u00b4 \u055e)\u0a0a( \u055e )\uff1e\ufeff</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/377-xanandithras","name":"Xanandithras","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar377_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"427"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-05T04:33:37-07:00","id":106205,"title":"","content":"No, nothing &quot;awesome.&quot;<br /> <br /> Stigmatic gets taken to Faerie, turned into a changeling, loses connection to Stigmatic-hood and G-M connections. Fetch remains, lacks Stigmatic-hood. Changeling returns, kills fetch, resumes life, joins freehold, lives in fear of Gentry. Same thing happens to ghouls, wolf-bloods, or proximi taken by Gentry; roughly the same thing happens if a stigmatic is Embraced or Awakens, but with joining the nightlife or council instead of freehold.<br /> <br /> This is the Demon forum. Can we talk about Demon instead of Changeling? This kind of question should really be in either that forum, or WoD general, as this is a crossover question. And, pretty much, all crossover questions always come down to ST fiat. The only awesome things that could happen are whatever the ST decides he wants to happen as a matter of plot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-05T11:02:34-07:00","id":106389,"title":"","content":"It all depends if you have a Gentry vs. God-Machine conflict in your head-canon (such as I do).<br /> <br /> Stigmatics could be recruited by Gentry, just as the Ensorcelled could be recruited by Angels.<br /> <br /> If they're Kept, as MCN said, I would imagine they would become Changelings before long. However, adhering to Rule #2, there's no reason the new Changelings can't create a Contract of Gears or Contract of Elements: Aether. To placate people with MCN's stance, Demons could have Fallen when trying to reclaim beings stolen by the Gentry, or tempted away from their mission.<br /> <br /> Honestly, the Gentry might be seeking to create these Contracts, or to sign deals with the God-Machine itself.<br /> <br /> Potential plot: Previously-reliable Stigmatics and information brokers go missing. The Ring is approached by a perfectly-normal-looking person they may have seen around saying they know where the missing people are, the PCs just need to bring ultra-strength Round-Up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Once is happenstance. Twice is coincidence. Three times is enemy action. Four times is Infrastructure.<br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> Rule #2: Never let the game-mechanics get in the way of a good story.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1642-paddon","name":"Paddon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1642_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"326"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-05T16:14:29-07:00","id":106595,"title":"","content":"Nothing special happens, I'd say. You have a Changeling that has a leftover Stigmatic mark incorporated into their Mien, but they are mechanically just another one of the Lost.<br /> <br /> That said, the God-Machine would almost certainly have an Angel watching over them, as they have to be an irregularity that promises interesting new data. I can imagine a few Inquisitors watching over them as well, potentially trying to indoctrinate them to their side of the conflict.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-05T21:12:23-07:00","id":106705,"title":"","content":"Contracts of Elements or Communion for Aether sounds like an interesting way to go about it actually. That and maybe a new Kith?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1734-asaram","name":"Asaram","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1734_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"331"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}